cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this Lean formalization, please cite this software release. Cite the article separately for its mathematical results."
type: software
title: "P1: Lean formalization of Sharp Poisson approximation and second-order correction for long multiplicative runs"
authors:
  - family-names: Pouly
    given-names: Brice
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-8491-2467"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-14"
url: "https://github.com/Vulkin-prog/paper-p1-lean"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Vulkin-prog/paper-p1-lean"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Lean v4.36.0-rc2 formalization and checked correspondence for the P1 article
  and its technical companion (26 and 92 numbered results respectively).
  Printed conditional hypotheses, including the order-254 input in main
  Theorem 5.2, are retained. Five issued Palomar records cover all 26 main
  results through 42 selected statements; companion Propositions T13.1 and
  T15.1 and the latter's displayed sequence corollary are directly selected
  in the fifth record. The remaining companion results are not separately
  claimed as registered. Mathematical and editorial assistance from
  ChatGPT (GPT-6 Astra) and Lean assistance from Codex are documented in the
  repository and manuscripts. Brice Pouly is the responsible human author.
  Apache-2.0 describes the software; preserved manuscripts and third-party
  material retain their own rights notices (see LICENSE_SCOPE.md).
keywords:
  - Lean
  - formalized mathematics
  - Poisson approximation
  - random multiplicative functions
  - factorial cumulants
  - Palomar
